<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 1.25 bln stg assistance.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 1.25 bln stg assistance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with assistance totalling 1.25 billion stg in its initial round of operations.  </p>
<p>The Bank provided 1.135 billion stg in fixed rate repos to March 19 and 20 at an unchanged 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>It also bought 115 million stg of bills maturing on or before March 20.</p>
<p>Its initial shortage forecast was 1.8 billion stg.</p>
</text>
